{
  "$comment": [
    "FactLens model registry -- the manifest described in the proposal's",
    "'Versioning and the model registry' section. It is loaded at application",
    "start and the active version is written into every model_runs row.",
    "",
    "HOW TO ACTIVATE A MODEL",
    "-----------------------",
    "1. Train and evaluate in training/, then export to ONNX.",
    "2. Copy the .onnx file and its tokenizer directory under models/.",
    "3. Fill in 'artifact', 'version', 'metrics', 'decision_threshold' and",
    "   'exported_at' in that model's entry below, and set 'registered': true.",
    "4. Restart the service, or POST /api/v1/admin/registry/reload.",
    "",
    "An entry whose 'artifact' is null -- or whose artifact file is missing --",
    "makes its provider report unavailable. The owning module then runs on its",
    "non-ML signals and marks the scan PARTIAL. That is the designed degraded",
    "mode, not a failure, and it is what all three models are in right now.",
    "",
    "A model is only accepted for integration when its external-set Macro F1",
    "is within the declared margin of its in-distribution score (see",
    "acceptance_policy below). Record both numbers in 'metrics'."
  ],
  "registry_version": "1.0.0",
  "updated_at": "2026-11-13",
  "acceptance_policy": {
    "max_external_macro_f1_drop": 0.1,
    "note": "A model scoring 0.95 in-distribution and 0.60 externally is overfitted to its corpus and is not shipped, regardless of how good the first number looks. The margin is declared here so the Phase 2 gate is checkable rather than rhetorical."
  },
